capability lz4/piece-decompress  a frame decompressed piece by piece in memory
  heroes  compress/lz4.Decompressor, compress/lz4.decompressor, compress/lz4.decompress_part, compress/lz4.with_dictionary
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  lz4.frame.LZ4FrameDecompressor, LZ4FrameDecompressor.decompress, LZ4FrameDecompressor.needs_input, lz4.frame.create_decompression_context, lz4.frame.decompress_chunk
  odin    -
  note    Python's `needs_input` is an answer of no bytes before `is_decompressor_ended`

capability lz4/stream-write  a frame written through a stream
  heroes  compress/lz4.Writer, compress/lz4.writer, compress/lz4.write, compress/lz4.flush, compress/lz4.finish
  go      NewWriter, Writer.Write, Writer.Flush, Writer.Close
  rust    FrameEncoder::flush, FrameEncoder::try_finish, FrameEncoder::get_ref, FrameEncoder::get_mut, FrameEncoder::into_inner, FrameEncoder::frame_info, FrameEncoder::auto_finish, frame::AutoFinishEncoder
  python  LZ4FrameFile.write, LZ4FrameFile.flush, LZ4FrameFile.close (mode 'wb'), auto_flush
  odin    -
  note    Python's `auto_flush` is a `flush` after each `write`; the stream is never closed by the writer, as Rust's `into_inner` hands it back

