capability lz4/compressing-reader  a reader that answers compressed bytes of what it reads
  heroes  compress/lz4.compressor, compress/lz4.compress_part
  go      CompressingReader, NewCompressingReader, CompressingReader.Read, CompressingReader.Close, CompressingReader.Source, CompressingReader.Apply, CompressingReader.Reset
  rust    -
  python  -
  odin    -
  note    a reader that answers compressed bytes is a `Compressor` fed what the program reads; Heroes has no interface for it to stand behind

capability lz4/concurrency  the blocks of a frame compressed on several threads
  heroes  refused: a thread carries one `i64` or one `str` (spec section 13), so a block cannot reach another thread but as text written and read back, which costs what the thread would save
  go      ConcurrencyOption, DefaultConcurrency
  rust    -
  python  -
  odin    -
  note    -

capability lz4/failures  what a broken block or frame answers
  heroes  compress/lz4.INVALID, compress/lz4.LIMIT, compress/lz4.CLOSED
  go      ErrInvalidFrame, ErrInternalUnhandledState, ErrOptionClosedOrError, ErrOptionNotApplicable, ErrWriterNotClosed, ErrWriterClosed
  rust    frame::Error, Error::CompressionError, Error::DecompressionError, Error::InvalidBlockInfo, Error::IoError, Error::ReservedBitsSet, Error::UnsupportedVersion, Error::WrongMagicNumber
  python  lz4.block.LZ4BlockError, RuntimeError
  odin    Error, General_Error, LZ4_Error
  note    `invalid` names the byte where the input stopped being LZ4

capability lz4/file  an LZ4 file opened by its path, read and written as a file
  heroes  refused: a path is `fs`'s, and a file's bytes are read whole by `fs.read_bytes` and written by `fs.write_bytes`, or streamed by `reader` and `writer` over `fs.open`
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  lz4.frame.open, lz4.frame.LZ4FrameFile, LZ4FrameFile.closed, LZ4FrameFile.close
  odin    -
  note    -

capability lz4/lines  a compressed text read line by line, or sought in
  heroes  refused: lines are `io`'s and `bytes.lines`'s over the bytes read whole; seeking is decompressing again from the start
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  LZ4FrameFile.readline, LZ4FrameFile.readlines, LZ4FrameFile.seek, LZ4FrameFile.tell, LZ4FrameFile.seekable
  odin    -
  note    -

dropped
  go      OnBlockDoneOption: a callback told of each block, a closure over the caller's state, which Heroes has not; a program feeding a `Compressor` sees each block as it goes
  go      Writer.Apply, Reader.Apply, Option, Option.String: options applied as functions after the object is made; Heroes's are a record given at once
  go      Writer.Reset, Reader.Reset, CompressingReader.Reset, LZ4FrameCompressor.reset, LZ4FrameDecompressor.reset, lz4.frame.reset_decompression_context: an object reused for another stream; a Heroes program makes a new value
  rust    block::CompressTable, CompressTable::Small, CompressTable::Large, CompressTable::small, CompressTable::large, block::compress_into_with_table: the size of the compressor's hash table, a memory knob
  rust    FrameInfo::new, FrameInfo::default and the builder setters: how Rust makes an options value; `default_options` and a record's fields here
  python  return_bytearray: which Python type the bytes come back as
  python  lz4.VERSION, lz4.version, lz4.library_version_number, lz4.library_version_string: which C library Python links; Rebel stands on none
  python  lz4.frame.builtins, lz4.frame.io, lz4.frame.lz4, lz4.frame.os, lz4.frame.sys: modules Python's `lz4.frame` imports
  python  LZ4FrameFile.fileno, LZ4FrameFile.isatty, LZ4FrameFile.readable, LZ4FrameFile.writable, LZ4FrameFile.detach, LZ4FrameFile.truncate, LZ4FrameFile.writelines: what every Python file object has
